  "body": "Test case -\r\n`data:text/html,<!doctype html><select multiple><option>a<br/>b</option><option></option></select><script>document.querySelector(\"select\").options[1].innerHTML=\"a<br/>b\";</script>`\r\nOr, if you prefer - https://jsfiddle.net/04brr6gj/\r\n\r\nIn all of the browsers, the first case (`<br/>` in the source) renders as `ab`.\r\nThe second case (`<br/>` using `innerHTML`) renders as\r\n```\r\na\r\nb\r\n```\r\nIn Firefox and as `ab` in the rest of the browsers.\r\n\r\nWhile I believe Firefox is inconsistent with itself and while I am not sure HTML specifies the rendering of form controls like `<select>`, I thought this might need a clarification.",
